  <page_number>37</page_number>
  <running_head>Theses Logicæ.</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">affirmatur etiam de integro secundum</l>
    <l n="2">partem.</l>
    <l n="3" para="true">181 Posito integro perfecto ponuntur</l>
    <l n="4">omnes ejus partes.</l>
    <l n="5" para="true">182 Posito integro imperfecto ponun-</l>
    <l n="6">tur omnes partes principales.</l>
    <l n="7" para="true">183 Sublata parte principali, tollitur</l>
    <l n="8">integrum.</l>
    <l n="9" para="true">184 Sublata parte qualibet, tollitur</l>
    <l n="10">perfectio integri.</l>
    <l n="11" para="true">185 Pars quæ dicitur singularis, qua</l>
    <l n="12">talis, est potius <i>species</i> quam membrum.</l>
    <l n="13" para="true">186 <i>Genus</i> est totum.</l>
    <l n="14" para="true">187 Ipsa natura generis simpliciter</l>
    <l n="15">consíderata, sine universalitate, est pars.</l>
    <l n="16" para="true">188 Genus &amp; universale idem sunt.</l>
    <l n="17" para="true">189 Genus existit extra intellectum.</l>
    <l n="18" para="true">190 Genus non existit extra suas species.</l>
    <l n="19" para="true">191 Genus nihil aliud est quam com-</l>
    <l n="20">munis illa natura, quæ variis rebus inest.</l>
    <l n="21" para="true">192 Quicquid essentiale affirmatur &amp;</l>
    <l n="22">negatur de genere, affirmatur etiam &amp;</l>
    <l n="23">negatur de specie.</l>
    <l n="24" para="true">193 Sublato genere tollitur species.</l>
    <l n="25" para="true">194 Posito genere ponitur aliqua spe-</l>
    <l n="26">cies.</l>
    <l n="27" para="true">195 Posita specie necessariò ponitur</l>
    <l n="28">genus.</l>
    <l n="29" para="true">196</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Left-edge fragment of facing page omitted. Some words are smudged (e.g. "consíderata", "universalitate" partly obscured); readings of 187 and 190 are doubtful, "extra" in 189 and "non" in 190 read with uncertainty.</notes>
